            <ArticleTitle>Ovarian remnant syndrome: a case report and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>121-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The ovarian remnant syndrome in an unusual complication of bilateral oophorectomy, usually presenting with pelvic mass and pain. A case of the syndrome is described in a 35-year-old woman with a history of abdominal hysterectomy and bilateral oophorectomy. We suggest that ovarian remnant syndrome should be considered in the differential diagnosis of chronic pelvic pain after recorded oophorectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
